Z||000000||phillip||06-29-2000||10:56 AM||||<BR>i had said i'd make it to the louisville show cause i am here and didn't trust my fiero go anywhere out of town. well, i guess i offended it. i've got something wrong engine wise that seems pretty serious. i really did want to drive it there since i can't do pics and i guess you get tired of me trying to describe things i've done to it. maybe by then i'll have it repaired but if you see about the 2nd most ragged s-10 blazer on the road with a much better set of wheels than it should have on it, i'm not there to steal parts off your cars, it's me.<P>so far i've just replaced plugs and wires, no improvement. guess i need a scan tool. i hate taking it to a garage and finding out it was something i could have done myself.<P>as for the problem: it "chugs" like one cylinder isn't firing. it also smells real "carbony" can a faulty o2 sensor cause that? it seems i end up needing a new one every year, but i don't want to keep guessing at components.<P>maybe get a compression guage to see if i've lost a cyl? <P>it sounds like my '84. when i got it the owner said he was told by the dealer it needed a head gasket. i've been trying to find out how to know that for sure. for now i have two non-running fieros. plus i hate the idea of putting a lot of money into the engine that could be going toward some thing better.<P>sorry this is long but engine problems always worry me.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||06-29-2000||12:26 PM||||head gaskets give a couple of signs. Funky color smoke from coolant and/or oil getting into the cylinder. Losing coolant/oil constantly (maybe not very fast, but still going down) if you change the oil and you find coolant it could be the head gasket. I'd say, start simple, just pull the plug wires, 1 at a time, and see if you find one that doesn't make it worse (ie: that plug might not be firing anyways) then, pull the plug, see what it looks like, oily? burnt up? nice and happy tan? throw a compression tester on it. if all that seems good, I'd say check the distributer cap for cracks (they can be kinda hard to see, pull it off and look on the inside) also look at the connectors, if they're looking carbon coated or mangled, time to get a new one (don't worry, they're reletively cheep) check the rotor while you have the dist cap off, is it still in good condition? once again a cheep thing to replace. Basically, just try the generic 'cure-all' of a tune up, new plugs, wires, rotor, cap, PCV, and an oil change, I just did mine and it came out to like $50 in parts, vice the $200+ the shop wanted. After that I would guess EGR just because I always hear about people having problems with them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||06-29-2000||01:10 PM||||Phillip, go to AutoZone and get one of the code readers and key -- you really need to know what is going in there......hate to hear that you are having probs, it's no fun, I know!! I will be getting in at the Ramada on Friday night if you want to stop by, just ask at the desk for Terry Owens........it would be good to see you there......<P>I will mention one other thing -- I had a prob with my V-6 that would act somewhat like what you are describing.......turned out to be a busted coolant sensor ...... you might check that......mine was stalling at red lights and stop signs and running rich, when it would restart it would act like it was flooded and then blow black smoke out the tailpipe.........these little cars are funny sometimes, one little problem will cause the whole system to act up -- the coolent sensor showed up with the scantool (code reader).....you should have one in your tool box anyway.........||||reg||1
Z||000003||phillip||06-30-2000||11:44 AM||||thanks for the ideas. got a 4 day weekend, maybe i can figure out something.<P>just to point out. mine is a project car/ daily driver. i don't want to give the impression that there is something special about it (if you see it that will be glaringly ovious). but since we discuss various mods and i've made attempts at them some of them (stereo mods, a-pillar guages, etc.), i thought of showing up as being a bit of contribution back to the forum since i can't do pics. i really do appreciate what i pick up here. <P>and when i say i hate putting money into the engine i mean this engine. if it gets costly i'll be wishing it were going toward a better drivetrain. thanks again.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-30-2000||12:21 PM||||Speaking of being jinxed...I <B>refuse</B> to drive around without my sunroof in place.  The Monkeymobile (now deceased)  :::moment of silence:::  never ran well, but it did run (with only a slow tranny and oil leak) until the day I removed the sunroof.  I drove all around town with the thing out.  That night she passed away.  (The oil puddle looked like Lake Erie. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)  I don't care if I get a brand new motor/tranny in the Grape Ape, the sunroof <B>WILL NOT</B> come out while I'm driving.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
