Z||000006||BAM-BAM||07-02-2000||11:20 AM||||   Phillip, I had similar problem(s) with my 85GT. I wound up replacing almost everything; wires, plugs, cap, rotor, IAC, TPS, O2, and the temp sensor. I figured the car was fourteen years old at the time, so what the heck. As soon as it sarted there was a noticalbe difference in everything from idle to power on acceleration. It still runs a little rich though, maybe I'll replace the air charge sensor next. Just a thought. Terry was right, one small thing can manefest itself as a major problem completely unrelated to itself. Good luck and let us know.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
